---
source: text/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"line\")"
---
Read one line from standard input and write it to standard output.

Reads byte-by-byte directly from FD 0 (no `BufReader`) so that chained invocations like `(line &&
line) <pipe` consume exactly one line each — a buffered reader would over-read and steal the rest
from the next process.

Behaviour matches POSIX: - exit 0 if a `\n` is read and echoed - exit 1 if EOF is hit before a `\n`;
a trailing `\n` is added to stdout in that case

Extra positional arguments are ignored to match upstream `line(1)` (the test harness sometimes
passes the literal string `line` as a buffer-size hint).

Usage: line

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
